  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MERT UN AFG 2015 - 2017</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">MERT UN AFG 2015 - 2017</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Provide 8 advanced life support flight qualified paramedics to provide 24/7 emergency medical intervention to UN and INGO staff (and in extremis support to partners and donors). 2. Provide an emergency medical officer to be located in Kabul to support and coordinate medical emergency intervention with aero-medical evacuation of injured or ill UN and INGO staff. 3. Emergency Medical courses will be conducted by the MERT personnel as part of their normal duties (at no additional cost) it is expected that Two (2) Training sessions should be provided at each location per month; one will involve capacity building for major health institutions in medical procedures and one will be general first aid training to UN and INGO staff in each location. 4. Mass casualty plans for all UN compounds will be reviewed by the MERT personnel and where possible rehearsals will be conducted of the plans. 5. The MERT personnel should assist the major medical facilities (hospitals or medical centres) in their location to review mass casualty response preparedness and response capacity, develop/review mass casualty plans and provide training to the emergency staff and facility managers on mass casualty preparedness and response. 6. All medical staff must be fluent in English (oral and written) 7. Reporting: the United Nations will require monthly reports on MERT / Medical Officer activities. These should be submitted with in conjunction with invoices.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">De internationella stridande trupperna har de senaste &#xe5;ren minskat sin n&#xe4;rvaro i Afghanistan, d&#xe4;rmed f&#xf6;rsvinner ocks&#xe5; mycket av den kvalificerade akutsjukv&#xe5;rden. Insatsen t&#xe4;cker delvis upp f&#xf6;r den f&#xf6;rlusten och erbjuder FN personal, humanit&#xe4;r personal, internationella NGOs, samt &#xe4;ven internationella givare tillg&#xe5;ng till MERT team (Medical Emergancy Response Team) i f&#xf6;ljande st&#xe4;der - Gardiz, Lashkar Gah, Herat, Jalalabad, Mazar, Fayzabad, Maimana och Bamyan.

MERT erbjuder 8 flygplan med kvalificerad ambulanspersonal med specialiserad och avancerad akutsjukv&#xe5;rd inom de f&#xf6;rsta kritiska 72 timmarna. Vidare erbjuder MERT team utbildning inom akutsjukv&#xe5;rd till de st&#xf6;rsta befintliga h&#xe4;lsov&#xe5;rdsinr&#xe4;ttningarna, samt utbildning i f&#xf6;rsta hj&#xe4;lpen till FN-personal och internationella NGOs p&#xe5; plats i ovan n&#xe4;mnda st&#xe4;der. MERT har dessutom en samordnare inom akutsjukv&#xe5;rd stationerad i Kabul. MERT &#xe4;r uppbyggd efter en modell som tidigare har testats i Somalia.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Medical Emergency Response Team (MERT)                                 Trauma Care, Stabilisation and Medevac Support</narrative>
  </description>
